    INCLUDING OF MERCHANTABILITY, SATISFACTORY QUALITY AND FITNESS FOR A
    PARTICULAR PURPOSE. Please see the CERN-OHL-S v2 for applicable conditions.

    Source location: https://github.com/copperheadhq/copperhead-555-oscillator

CERN-OHL-S is *strongly reciprocal*: if you distribute a product made from a modified version
of this design, you must make the complete modified source available under the same licence.

## Documentation: CC-BY-4.0

Applies to: `docs/`, `images/`, `README.md` and the README files in each directory.

Share and adapt freely, with attribution.

## Not covered by any of the above

**The copperhead logo.** `images/copperhead-lockup.png` and `images/copperhead-lockup-light.png`
come from https://github.com/copperheadhq/copperhead-site (`branding/png/`). They identify
Copperhead and are not covered by CC-BY-4.0; do not use them to imply endorsement or
affiliation.

**Third-party libraries.** Footprints and symbols in `hardware/` derive from the KiCad
standard libraries, which carry their own licence (CC-BY-SA 4.0 with an exception for use in
designs; see https://www.kicad.org/libraries/license/). That exception is why boards using
them, including this one, are not forced to CC-BY-SA.

**Component 3D models.** Most models inside the files in `3d/` and the renders in `images/`
come from the KiCad standard library and are generic package bodies, not the exact
manufacturer parts. The model for SW1 in `hardware/lib/ck_switches.3dshapes/` was fetched
from EasyEDA/LCSC (C221661) and remains under its publisher's terms; it is not relicensed
here. The SW1 footprint in `hardware/lib/ck_switches.pretty/` was drawn for this project
from the C&K drawing (sheet I-53) and is covered by CERN-OHL-S-2.0 with the rest of
`hardware/`.
